<div class="form-note u-pad-1-4_1-6 u-fs-1 eo-staging-note"><strong>Interactive map coming to this preview.</strong> The live site’s municipal equality map is an interactive tool — a statewide map embed plus individual detail pages for the more than 250 Ohio cities whose codes Equality Ohio analyzed. It isn’t recreated in this design preview yet; per‑city protection data returns here as a Supabase‑driven feature, so each city’s page can be updated without a redeploy. In the meantime, explore the current map on the live site: <a href="https://equalityohio.org/our-work/local/municipal-map/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">equalityohio.org/our-work/local/municipal-map</a>.</div>
<!-- /wp:eo/text -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"mt-2 u-maxw-62"} -->
<p class="mt-2 u-maxw-62">Ohio doesn’t have statewide, comprehensive laws prohibiting discrimination against LGBTQ+ people yet. There are also no laws banning conversion “therapy” on minors throughout the state. However, the local municipalities listed above have done the work themselves, and passed these or other laws protecting LGBTQ+ people from discrimination.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"u-maxw-62"} -->
<p class="u-maxw-62"><strong>Ohio is one of 29 states that leaves LGBTQ people out of laws that make discrimination illegal.</strong> However, some individual communities have enacted these protections themselves.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"u-maxw-62"} -->
<p class="u-maxw-62"><strong>Equality Ohio performed an analysis on the city codes of over 250 Ohio cities for this map.</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
